// Cluster library: small hand-composed scenes the decorator places as one unit.
// Item: [key, x, z, size, rotation (degrees), solid?, y]
//   key   — "<kit>/<model>" under assets/ (kits: survival, pirate, castle, town, nature, plus the older packs)
//   x, z  — metres from the cluster centre; +z points "forward" (towards the path the cluster faces)
//   size  — largest dimension in metres (same rule as model() in the game)
//   solid — blocks movement and bullets (default true; false for grass, flowers, small clutter)
//   y     — lift in metres for stacked pieces (second storeys, roofs); default 0
// Orientation: Kenney siege machines (catapult, trebuchet, ballista, ram, siege tower) face +x and pirate cannons
// face −z in their own models; items here turn them (−90° / 180°) so they aim at the cluster front (+z).
// Cluster fields: name (ru), themes, place (where the decorator may put it), radius (footprint, m),
//   tints (optional) — { modelKey: 0xRRGGBB } recolours every copy of that model in the cluster.
//   pads (optional) — jump pads that come with the cluster: { x, z, tier, speed, role, target: [x, y, z] }
//     tier: "spring" (light hop), "blue" (medium), "yellow" (high) — see PAD_TIERS in engine/jump-pad.js
//     in the same local metres; `target` is where the jump should land (for the preview arc and later checks).
//   previewYaw / previewPitch (optional) — catalogue camera angles in degrees (defaults 45 / 35).
//   explosive (optional) — model keys in this cluster that are powder barrels: they blow up like red crates.
//   place: "open" — free ground; "edge" — back to a wall or arena edge; "path" — beside a route;
//          "corner" — inside a corner; "focal" — centre of a plaza.
